From 67610695e59ea2e75a81b7d55daa7fc9bddf1b89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:30:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Demo tunes in data/music, so MidiPlayer has something to play

Nothing in the image was a .mid, so MidiPlayer opened to an empty file
picker -- and until the soundfont went in (patch 0046) it could not have
played one anyway.

Three short arrangements, written by HaikuArmQemu's tools/music/tunes.py
rather than downloaded, so their provenance is plain and they can be
regenerated: Beethoven's Fur Elise (1810) and the Ode to Joy theme
(1824), and Pachelbel's Canon in D (before 1706) with its ground bass and
three canonic entries. All are long out of copyright.

They are arrangements by ear, not urtext transcriptions: enough to
recognise the tune, to exercise the General MIDI soundfont, and -- with
MidiPlayer's output switched to /dev/midi/prose/0 -- to play through the
Mac's synth instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0047-demo-tunes-in-data-music-so-midiplayer-has-something-to-play.patch 253901be5d2ff79be7c8cd134e70b8d7217973b3c2aae1e28954349023e53a86
---
 build/jam/packages/Haiku              |  10 ++++++++++
 data/music/Beethoven - Fur Elise.mid  | Bin 0 -> 983 bytes
 data/music/Beethoven - Ode to Joy.mid | Bin 0 -> 517 bytes
 data/music/Pachelbel - Canon in D.mid | Bin 0 -> 2689 bytes
 4 files changed, 10 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 data/music/Beethoven - Fur Elise.mid
 create mode 100644 data/music/Beethoven - Ode to Joy.mid
 create mode 100644 data/music/Pachelbel - Canon in D.mid

diff --git a/build/jam/packages/Haiku b/build/jam/packages/Haiku
index 5843b0b90e..06104f23df 100644
--- a/build/jam/packages/Haiku
+++ b/build/jam/packages/Haiku
@@ -286,6 +286,16 @@ local logoArtwork =
 SEARCH on $(logoArtwork) = [ FDirName $(HAIKU_TOP) data artwork ] ;
 AddFilesToPackage data artwork : $(logoArtwork) ;
 
+# PROSE fork: demo tunes for MidiPlayer, which otherwise opens to an empty
+# file picker -- nothing else in the image is a .mid. Written by
+# HaikuArmQemu's tools/music/tunes.py; every piece is long out of copyright.
+local demoTunes =
+	"Beethoven - Fur Elise.mid"
+	"Beethoven - Ode to Joy.mid"
+	"Pachelbel - Canon in D.mid" ;
+SEARCH on $(demoTunes) = [ FDirName $(HAIKU_TOP) data music ] ;
+AddFilesToPackage data music : $(demoTunes) ;
+
 # Mail spell check dictionaries
 local spellFiles = words geekspeak ;
 spellFiles = $(spellFiles:G=spell) ;
